('a9ed7ce7-1bf3-5616-9133-9a20a06acb4b', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 26, 26, 'An echo sounder must detect objects up to 15 cm deep in tissue (v = 1540 m s⁻¹). What is the greatest pulse repetition frequency it can use, in kHz?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '5.133 kHz', 'kHz', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Round trip time = 2 × 0.15 ÷ 1540 = 1.948 × 10⁻⁴ s. f = 1 ÷ 1.948 × 10⁻⁴ = 5133 Hz. In kHz: 5133 ÷ 10³ = 5.13. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: round-trip time. C1: f = 1/t. A1: f = 5.13 kHz.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('cdaaafdf-1824-5bd2-98dd-60003beff94d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 27, 27, 'An echo appears earlier on an A-scan than expected because the tissue has a higher speed of sound than assumed. What effect does this have on the measured depth?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The calculated depth is smaller than the real depth', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The machine uses an assumed v; a faster medium returns echoes sooner. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: shorter time. C1: underestimate. A1: B (The calculated depth is smaller than the real depth).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('04ad3edb-2dab-5097-9e63-89bd7ab07e4d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 28, 28, 'For ultrasound of wavelength 0.40 mm, the smallest separation of two boundaries that can be distinguished is about half a wavelength. Calculate this separation in mm.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.2 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Separation ≈ λ/2 = 0.40 ÷ 2 = 0.20 mm. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: λ/2. C1: value. A1: Δx = 0.20 mm.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ecc24d2a-cfe2-5c67-902c-68c65bb397a5', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 29, 29, 'An echo from the far side of a 4.0 cm thick organ returns 52 µs after the echo from its near side. Calculate the speed of ultrasound in the organ.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1538', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 2d/Δt = 2 × 0.040 ÷ 52 × 10⁻⁶ = 1540 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: extra path 2d. C1: Δt in s. C1: value. A1: v = 1540 m s⁻¹.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('468ab597-f119-5c19-8e6c-a161dd67eb4c', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 30, 30, 'Why can ultrasound not be used to image the lungs?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Air in the lungs reflects almost all the ultrasound at the tissue boundary', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The impedance mismatch between tissue and air is enormous. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: air in lungs. C1: total reflection. A1: C (Air in the lungs reflects almost all the ultrasound at the tissue boundary).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e417685d-c672-5a90-a5ab-d70143442aa7', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 31, 31, 'A ship sends a sonar pulse; the echo from a shoal returns after 0.18 s and the echo from the sea bed after 0.52 s. Sound travels at 1500 m s⁻¹ in the sea. Calculate the distance between the shoal and the sea bed.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '255', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'd = 1500 × (0.52 − 0.18) ÷ 2 = 255 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: time difference. C1: d = vΔt/2. A1: d = 255 m.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgffe183c8-t fgffe183c8-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgffe183c8-t">Shoal and sea bed</title><desc id="fgffe183c8-d">A ship''s sonar pulse gives an echo from a shoal of fish after 0.18 s and from the sea bed after 0.52 s.</desc><line x1="20" y1="60" x2="400" y2="60" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,58 270,58 255,74 165,74" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="195" y="38" width="30" height="20" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="200" y1="76" x2="200" y2="211.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,216 197,209.7 203,209.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="220" y1="216" x2="220" y2="80.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="220,76 223,82.3 217,82.3" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><path d="M20,220 Q120,210 210,220 T400,224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="390" y="238" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">sea bed</text><text x="240" y="110" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">shoal: 0.18 s</text><text x="240" y="190" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">sea bed: 0.52 s</text></svg>', 'A ship''s sonar pulse gives an echo from a shoal of fish after 0.18 s and from the sea bed after 0.52 s.'),
('253ef62c-b7ff-5fe7-a227-38fd137af184', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 32, 32, 'The A-scan time base is 10 µs per division. An echo is 6.4 divisions after the pulse, and v = 1540 m s⁻¹. Calculate the depth in mm.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '49.28 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 6.4 × 10 = 64 µs. d = 1540 × 64 × 10⁻⁶ ÷ 2 = 0.04928 m. In mm: 0.04928 × 10³ = 49.3. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: time from trace. C1: d = vt/2. A1: d = 49.3 mm.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgcfae9e71-t fgcfae9e71-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgcfae9e71-t">A-scan trace</title><desc id="fgcfae9e71-d">A-scan trace with a time base of 10 µs per division: the transmitted pulse at 0 and an echo 6.4 divisions later.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="106.8" y1="34" x2="106.8" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180.6" y1="34" x2="180.6" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="254.4" y1="34" x2="254.4" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="328.2" y1="34" x2="328.2" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="402" y1="34" x2="402" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="33" y1="192" x2="402" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#