('85cd25cc-d76b-511e-bce6-27cd5deeaf91', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 33, 33, 'A boundary deep in the body gives a much smaller echo than an identical boundary near the surface. Why?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'The ultrasound is attenuated on its longer path there and back', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Intensity falls exponentially with distance travelled. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: attenuation. C1: longer path. A1: A (The ultrasound is attenuated on its longer path there and back).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('188da8bd-f67f-5f7b-abaf-966707cbc2da', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 34, 34, 'A dolphin hears the echo of its click from a fish 0.040 s after sending it. Sound travels at 1500 m s⁻¹ in sea water. How far away is the fish?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '30', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'd = 1500 × 0.040 ÷ 2 = 30 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: round trip. C1: value. A1: d = 30 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ca6a8981-3f24-5533-b7f8-879b7fc8af13', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 35, 35, 'An echo sounder uses 50 kHz pulses in water (v = 1500 m s⁻¹). Each pulse lasts 10 cycles. Calculate the shortest distance between two objects along the beam whose echoes do not overlap, in cm.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '15 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Pulse length in time = 10 ÷ 50 × 10³ = 2.0 × 10⁻⁴ s. Separation = 1500 × 2.0 × 10⁻⁴ ÷ 2 = 0.1500 m. In cm: 0.1500 × 100 = 15.0. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: pulse duration. M1: echoes separated by more than the pulse. C1: halve for round trip. A1: Δd = 15 cm.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('15f16ba7-ef22-5271-bb04-d2acfe261a70', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 36, 36, 'In an A-scan, the first large peak at time zero is', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'the transmitted pulse itself (and the echo from the skin surface)', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Echo times are measured from this reference. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: transmitted pulse. C1: reference time. A1: D (the transmitted pulse itself (and the echo from the skin surface)).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('e4f9ec18-f7d1-51b5-86c6-0ed45ace3a28', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 37, 37, 'In an echo-location test, a pulse is sent towards a cliff 510 m away and the echo heard 3.0 s later. Calculate the speed of sound in air.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '340', 'm s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'v = 2d/t = 2 × 510 ÷ 3.0 = 340 m s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: round trip. C1: value. A1: v = 340 m s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('243ec66e-cf16-5045-990c-3d641942dcc5', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 38, 38, 'An echo returns from the back of an eye 30 µs after the echo from the front. The speed of sound in the eye is 1530 m s⁻¹. Calculate the length of the eye in mm.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '22.95 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'L = 1530 × 30 × 10⁻⁶ ÷ 2 = 0.02295 m. In mm: 0.02295 × 10³ = 23.0. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: d = vΔt/2. C1: m to mm. A1: L = 23.0 mm.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('74218419-895c-5ab8-bb3e-f1b886039c8e', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 39, 39, 'An A-scan machine amplifies later echoes more than early ones (time-gain compensation). Why?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'To make up for the extra attenuation suffered by echoes from deeper boundaries', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Equal boundaries then give similar peak heights at any depth. Mark scheme (4 marks). C1: attenuation with depth. C1: gain increases with time. C1: comparable echoes. A1: B (To make up for the extra attenuation suffered by echoes from deeper boundaries).', 4, NULL, NULL),
('3ae7391f-49d9-5b54-a180-ca6493fafc0e', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 40, 40, 'A parking sensor emits 40 kHz pulses and detects an echo from a wall after 6.0 ms. Sound travels at 340 m s⁻¹. How far away is the wall, in cm?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '102 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'd = 340 × 6.0 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2 = 1.02 m. In cm: 1.02 × 100 = 102. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: d = vt/2. C1: ms and cm. A1: d = 102 cm.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('ce9a5de2-a816-5d50-bd71-0bed023d119d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 41, 41, 'Calculate the time between an echo from a boundary 30 mm deep and one from a boundary 50 mm deep, in tissue with v = 1500 m s⁻¹, in µs.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '26.67 us', 'µs', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δt = 2 × (0.050 − 0.030) ÷ 1500 = 2.67 × 10⁻⁵ s. In µs: 2.67 × 10⁻⁵ × 10⁶ = 26.7. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: depth difference. C1: Δt = 2Δd/v. A1: Δt = 26.7 µs.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('22715651-ead4-5a80-9c5d-0504f2838d2d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 42, 42, 'Why does echo sounding at sea use much lower frequencies than medical ultrasound?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Lower frequencies are attenuated less, so they travel the much greater distances needed', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Range matters more than resolution at sea. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: attenuation rises with f. C1: long range needed. A1: C (Lower frequencies are attenuated less, so they travel the much greater distances needed).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('78e36246-f8c2-5f15-9849-7301282e7406', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 43, 43, 'An A-scan of an eye shows echoes at 8.0 µs (front of lens), 13.2 µs (back of lens) and 31.0 µs (retina). The speed of sound is 1640 m s⁻¹ in the lens and 1530 m s⁻¹ elsewhere in the eye. (a) Calculate the thickness of the lens. (b) Calculate the distance from the back of the lens to the retina. Give only the answer to (b), in mm.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '13.62 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 1640 × 5.2 × 10⁻⁶ ÷ 2 = 0.004264 m. (b) 1530 × (31.0 − 13.2) × 10⁻⁶ ÷ 2 = 0.01362 m. In mm: 0.01362 × 10³ = 13.6. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: lens thickness. M1: time difference for vitreous. C1: d = vt/2. C1: value. A1: d = 13.6 mm.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="fge130b2b2-t fge130b2b2-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fge130b2b2-t">A-scan of an eye</title><desc id="fge130b2b2-d">A-scan of an eye: the transmitted pulse at 0 and echoes at 8.0 µs (front of lens), 13.2 µs (back of lens) and 31.0 µs (retina).</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="125.3" y1="34" x2="125.3" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="217.5" y1="34" x2="217.5" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="309.8" y1="34" x2="309.8" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="402" y1="34" x2="402" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-