('451f06ac-2802-5b50-aa40-507eda7cae5e', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 44, 44, 'An echo sounder on a boat sends pulses straight down. In shallow water the echo returns after 0.030 s; further out it returns after 0.090 s. Sound travels at 1500 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate the two depths. (b) The boat travels 400 m between the readings. Calculate the average gradient of the sea bed. (c) Calculate the largest pulse rate that can be used in the deeper water. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.1125', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 1500 × 0.030 ÷ 2 = 22.5 m and 1500 × 0.090 ÷ 2 = 67.5 m. (b) (67.5 − 22.5) ÷ 400 = 0.113. (c) 1 ÷ 0.090 = 11 pulses per second. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: first depth. C1: second depth. M1: rise ÷ run. C1: value. C1: pulse rate. A1: gradient = 0.113.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg8535e011-t fg8535e011-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg8535e011-t">Echo sounding from a boat</title><desc id="fg8535e011-d">A boat sends sonar pulses straight down to the sea bed; the echo time grows from 0.030 s to 0.090 s as the boat moves into deeper water.</desc><line x1="20" y1="60" x2="400" y2="60" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:1.4;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="150,58 270,58 255,74 165,74" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="195" y="38" width="30" height="20" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="200" y1="76" x2="200" y2="211.1" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="200,216 197,209.7 203,209.7" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="220" y1="216" x2="220" y2="80.9" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="220,76 223,82.3 217,82.3" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><path d="M20,220 Q120,210 210,220 T400,224" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><text x="390" y="238" font-size="12" text-anchor="end" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">sea bed</text><text x="240" y="140" font-size="12" text-anchor="start" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">0.030 s, then 0.090 s</text></svg>', 'A boat sends sonar pulses straight down to the sea bed; the echo time grows from 0.030 s to 0.090 s as the boat moves into deeper water.'),
('384b93ca-dd59-5343-8505-0f166024f637', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 45, 45, 'Ultrasound pulses of 3.0 MHz are used, each 4 cycles long, in tissue with v = 1540 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate the wavelength. (b) Calculate the pulse length in the tissue. (c) Estimate the smallest separation of two boundaries along the beam that can be resolved (half the pulse length), in mm.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.027 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) λ = 1540 ÷ 3.0 × 10⁶ = 5.133 × 10⁻⁴ m. (b) L = 4 × 5.133 × 10⁻⁴ = 0.002053 m. (c) 0.002053 ÷ 2 = 0.001027 m, which in mm is 0.001027 × 10³ = 1.03. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: λ. C1: pulse length. M1: half the pulse length. C1: value. A1: Δx = 1.03 mm.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('501e4cfb-6d1c-53ea-add8-4d69f91fcbf3', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 46, 46, 'A probe sends a pulse through 2.0 cm of fat (v = 1450 m s⁻¹) and then muscle (v = 1590 m s⁻¹). An echo from a bone boundary returns 80 µs after the pulse. (a) Calculate the time spent crossing the fat (both ways). (b) Calculate the depth of the bone below the fat–muscle boundary. Give only the answer to (b), in mm.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '41.67 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) t = 2 × 0.020 ÷ 1450 = 2.759 × 10⁻⁵ s. (b) Remaining time = 80 × 10⁻⁶ − 2.759 × 10⁻⁵ = 5.241 × 10⁻⁵ s; d = 1590 × 5.241 × 10⁻⁵ ÷ 2 = 0.04167 m. In mm: 0.04167 × 10³ = 41.7. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: time in fat. M1: subtract from total. C1: remaining time. C1: d = vt/2. C1: value. A1: d = 41.7 mm.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('b6aa5660-4e0c-53ea-8294-ed94080aa55c', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 47, 47, 'A bat flying at 5.0 m s⁻¹ towards a wall emits a click when it is 6.0 m away. Sound travels at 340 m s⁻¹. (a) Show that the bat travels much less than 6.0 m before the echo returns. (b) Calculate the echo time, ignoring the bat''s motion. Give only the answer to (b), in ms.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '35.29 ms', 'ms', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) In about 0.035 s it moves 5.0 × 0.035 ≈ 0.18 m. (b) t = 2 × 6.0 ÷ 340 = 0.03529 s. In ms: 0.03529 × 10³ = 35.3. Mark scheme (5 marks). B1: small distance moved. M1: t = 2d/v. C1: s to ms. C1: value. A1: t = 35.3 ms.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('017237f8-781d-5692-a6a9-4bc0ae7397b3', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 48, 48, 'The A-scan shows the transmitted pulse at 0, a peak at 26 µs and a peak at 91 µs; the time base is 13 µs per division. The speed of sound is 1540 m s⁻¹. (a) Calculate the positions of both peaks in divisions. (b) Calculate the depth of the deeper boundary in mm. (c) Calculate the separation of the boundaries. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '70.07 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 26 ÷ 13 = 2.0 and 91 ÷ 13 = 7.0 divisions. (b) d = 1540 × 91 × 10⁻⁶ ÷ 2 = 0.07007 m. In mm: 0.07007 × 10³ = 70.1. (c) 1540 × 65 × 10⁻⁶ ÷ 2 ≈ 50 mm. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: divisions. M1: d = vt/2. C1: substitution. C1: value. C1: separation. A1: d = 70.1 mm.', 6, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 420 240" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg928de16e-t fg928de16e-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg928de16e-t">A-scan trace</title><desc id="fg928de16e-d">A-scan trace: the transmitted pulse at 0 and echoes at 26 µs and 91 µs; the grid lines are 13 µs apart.</desc><line x1="33" y1="34" x2="33" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="69.9" y1="34" x2="69.9" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="106.8" y1="34" x2="106.8" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="143.7" y1="34" x2="143.7" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5db);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><line x1="180.6" y1="34" x2="180.6" y2="192" style="stroke:var(--fig-grid,#d1d5