192 373.7,192 374.1,192 374.5,192 374.9,192 375.4,192 375.8,192 376.2,192 376.6,192 377,192 377.4,192 377.8,192 378.2,192 378.6,192 379,192 379.5,192 379.9,192 380.3,192 380.7,192 381.1,192 381.5,192 381.9,192 382.3,192 382.7,192 383.1,192 383.6,192 384,192 384.4,192 384.8,192 385.2,192 385.6,192 386,192 386.4,192 386.8,192 387.2,192 387.7,192 388.1,192 388.5,192 388.9,192 389.3,192 389.7,192 390.1,192 390.5,192 390.9,192 391.3,192 391.8,192 392.2,192 392.6,192 393,192 393.4,192 393.8,192 394.2,192 394.6,192 395,192 395.4,192 395.9,192 396.3,192 396.7,192 397.1,192 397.5,192 397.9,192 398.3,192 398.7,192 399.1,192 399.5,192 400,192 400.4,192 400.8,192 401.2,192 401.6,192 402,192" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/></svg>', 'A-scan trace: the transmitted pulse at 0 and echoes at 26 µs and 91 µs; the grid lines are 13 µs apart.'),
('2965e456-1006-5dc3-9c01-e1262848d2b5', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 49, 49, 'An echo sounder is calibrated in fresh water (v = 1480 m s⁻¹) but used in sea water (v = 1520 m s⁻¹). It shows a depth of 74.0 m. (a) Calculate the echo time. (b) Calculate the true depth.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '76', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) t = 2 × 74.0 ÷ 1480 = 0.1000 s. (b) d = 1520 × 0.1000 ÷ 2 = 76.0 m. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: echo time from displayed depth. C1: value. M1: true speed. C1: value. A1: d = 76.0 m.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('65048247-37d8-5cfe-80f4-3b84977144f4', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', 'd8943c26-698b-4e81-97d1-7588165e9880', 'a-level', '30.6', '9702 coursebook 30.6 · Echo sounding', 50, 50, 'A transducer emits a pulse every 0.25 ms. (a) Calculate the pulse repetition frequency. (b) Calculate the greatest depth that can be imaged without echoes overlapping the next pulse, in tissue with v = 1540 m s⁻¹. Give only the answer to (b), in cm.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '19.25 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) f = 1 ÷ 0.25 × 10⁻³ = 4000 Hz. (b) d = 1540 × 0.25 × 10⁻³ ÷ 2 = 0.1925 m. In cm: 0.1925 × 100 = 19.2. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: f = 1/T. M1: echo must return within T. C1: d = vT/2. C1: m to cm. C1: value. A1: d(max) = 19.2 cm.', 6, NULL, NULL)
