('502b39a7-3b4e-575e-b264-9a5108658ca3', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '75e89d65-181a-4db5-a20b-511fa32bab7d', 'a-level', '30.7', '9702 coursebook 30.7 · Ultrasound scanning', 50, 50, 'In a scan, the echo from a liver–kidney boundary (α = 0.0060) is compared with the echo from a liver–bone boundary (α = 0.40) at the same depth. (a) Calculate (bone echo) ÷ (kidney echo). (b) Express this ratio in decibels. Give only the answer to (b).', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '18.24', 'dB', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 0.40 ÷ 0.0060 = 66.7. (b) 10 × lg(66.67) = 18.2 dB. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: ratio. M1: dB = 10 lg ratio. C1: substitution. C1: value. B1: same attenuation for same depth. A1: ratio = 18.2 dB.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('51994e99-7f1c-5412-ba9a-b43c5c8b621a', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '75e89d65-181a-4db5-a20b-511fa32bab7d', 'a-level', '30.7', '9702 coursebook 30.7 · Ultrasound scanning', 51, 51, 'Blood (Z = 1.66 × 10⁶ kg m⁻² s⁻¹) flows in a vessel surrounded by tissue (Z = 1.63 × 10⁶ kg m⁻² s⁻¹). (a) Calculate the reflection coefficient. (b) Calculate the echo intensity from an incident intensity of 0.20 W m⁻², in units of 10⁻⁵ W m⁻².', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.663', '10⁻⁵ W m⁻²', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) α = ((1.66 − 1.63) ÷ (1.66 + 1.63))² = 8.315 × 10⁻⁵. (b) 0.20 × 8.315 × 10⁻⁵ = 1.66 × 10⁻⁵ W m⁻². Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: α. M1: I = αI₀. C1: substitution. C1: value. A1: I = 1.66 × 10⁻⁵ W m⁻².', 5, NULL, NULL)
