t</text><line x1="61" y1="168" x2="299" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="199" y1="168" x2="68.6" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="63,168 70.3,164.6 70.3,171.4" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="211" y1="168" x2="291.4" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="297,168 289.7,171.4 289.7,164.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><circle cx="205" cy="168" r="5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="180" cy="168" r="2.4" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><text x="55" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><text x="305" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">B</text><text x="180" y="14" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280)">ring of detectors</text></svg>', 'End-on view of a PET detector ring around a patient, with two photons from an annihilation travelling in opposite directions to two detectors.'),
('22b3fd31-9318-583f-b8d4-d29d8b66fa24', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 21, 21, 'Two annihilation photons reach opposite detectors 400 ps apart. How far from the midpoint of the line between the detectors did the annihilation happen, in mm? Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '60 mm', 'mm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'd = cΔt/2 = 3.00 × 10⁸ × 400 × 10⁻¹² ÷ 2 = 0.060 m. In mm: 0.060 × 10³ = 60. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: d = cΔt/2. A1: d = 60 mm.', 2, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fgcff761a6-t fgcff761a6-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fgcff761a6-t">PET detector ring</title><desc id="fgcff761a6-d">End-on view of a PET detector ring. An annihilation off the centre sends two photons in opposite directions along the line of response to detectors A and B, arriving 400 ps apart.</desc><rect x="300" y="163" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="298.1" y="141.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="292.5" y="120.2" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="283.3" y="100.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="270.8" y="82.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="255.3" y="67.2" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="237.5" y="54.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="217.8" y="45.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="196.7" y="39.9" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="175" y="38" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="153.3" y="39.9" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="132.2" y="45.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="112.5" y="54.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="94.7" y="67.2" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="79.2" y="82.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="66.7" y="100.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="57.5" y="120.2" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="51.9" y="141.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="50" y="163" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="51.9" y="184.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="57.5" y="205.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="66.7" y="225.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="79.2" y="243.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="94.7" y="258.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="112.5" y="271.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="132.2" y="280.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="153.3" y="286.1" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="175" y="288" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="196.7" y="286.1" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="217.8" y="280.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="237.5" y="271.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="255.3" y="258.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="270.8" y="243.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="283.3" y="225.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="292.5" y="205.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="298.1" y="184.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="180" cy="168" r="60" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="180" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280)">patient</text><line x1="61" y1="168" x2="299" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="204" y1="168" x2="68.6" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="63,168 70.3,164.6 70.3,171.4" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="216" y1="168" x2="291.4" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="297,168 289.7,171.4 289.7,164.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><circle cx="210" cy="168" r="5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="180" cy="168" r="2.4" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><text x="55" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><text x="305" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">B</text><text x="180" y="14" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280)">ring of detectors</text><polygon points="180,194 186.3,191 186.3,197" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="184.9" y1="194" x2="205.1" y2="194" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="210,194 203.7,197 203.7,191" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="195" y="206" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">d</text></svg>', 'End-on view of a PET detector ring. An annihilation off the centre sends two photons in opposite directions along the line of response to detectors A and B, arriving 400 ps apart.'),
('0a579cd3-f1be-5d51-833c-76fa5c5990b9', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 22, 22, 'What does a PET image mainly show?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Where the tracer collects, showing how active tissues are', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'PET images function (metabolism), not just anatomy. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: D (Where the tracer collects, showing how active tissues are).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('2cebb8c4-7a91-583a-8543-ca640d65f96d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 23, 23, 'What fraction of a fluorine-18 dose (half-life 110 min) remains after 60 minutes?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.6852', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Fraction = 0.5^(60 ÷ 110) = 0.685. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: (½)^(t/t½). A1: fraction = 0.685.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('616a6a65-d6ff-50da-a21c-f6d1aa5336e4', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 24, 24, 'Roughly how far does a positron from a PET tracer travel before it annihilates?', NULL, 1, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'About a millimetre', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'It slows quickly in tissue, then meets an electron. Mark scheme (1 mark). B1: B (About a millimetre).', 1, NULL, NULL),
('66391574-2302-5a8a-ae89-85e2db275de1', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 25, 25, 'Each annihilation photon carries 0.511 MeV. Calculate the total energy of the two photons.', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.022', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = 2 × 0.511 = 1.022 MeV. Mark scheme (1 mark). A1: E = 1.022 MeV.', 1, NULL, NULL),
('75000de0-b809-5983-a843-3dfdc1366ba6', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 26, 26, 'A fluorine-18 dose has an activity of 600 MBq when injected. What is its activity after one half-life, 110 minutes later, in MBq?', NULL, 1, 'numeric'::answer_type, '300', 'MBq', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['3e8']::text[], 'One half-life halves the activity: A = 600 ÷ 2 = 300 MBq. Mark scheme (2 marks). C1: halve once. A1: A = 300 MBq.', 2, NULL, NULL),
('4ab3559e-ac82-5bac-b0b5-63ec0339a7a7', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 27, 27, 'A patient needs 370 MBq of fluorine-18 (half-life 110 min) at injection, which happens 2.0 hours after the tracer is made. What activity must be made, in MBq?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '788.1', 'MBq', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['7.881e8']::text[], 'A₀ = 370 × 2^(120 ÷ 110) = 788 MBq. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: hours to minutes. C1: A₀ = A × 2^(t/t½). A1: A₀ = 788 MBq.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f3e9834f-8e9a-51f3-84c9-a64812b5a8bf', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 28, 28, 'A fluorine-18 source (λ = 1.05 × 10⁻⁴ s⁻¹) has an activity of 400 MBq. How many fluorine-18 nuclei does it contain?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3.81e12', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'N = A/λ = 400 × 10⁶ ÷ 1.05 × 10⁻⁴ = 3.81 × 10¹². Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: MBq to Bq. C1: N = A/λ. A1: N = 3.81 × 10¹².', 3, NULL, NULL),
('3f323d8c-df43-5535-be9e-ddb1d57b5aa3', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 29, 29, 'Two opposite PET detectors record photons from an annihilation that took place 9.0 cm closer to one of them than the centre point. What is the gap between the two arrival times, in ps? Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '600', 'ps', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'One photon travels 0.090 m further and the other 0.090 m less: Δt = 2 × 0.090 ÷ 3.00 × 10⁸ = 6.0 × 10⁻¹⁰ s. In ps: 6.0 × 10⁻¹⁰ × 10¹² = 600. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: path difference 2d. C1: Δt = 2d/c. C1: s to ps. A1: Δt = 600 ps.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('d852c906-e13d-5943-9ab6-846eca784679', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 30, 30, 'After a PET scan, patients are told to drink plenty of water. Why?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Frequent urination removes the tracer from the bladder sooner, lowering the dose', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Excretion shortens the effective half-life. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: tracer excreted. C1: lower dose. A1: C (Frequent urination removes the tracer from the bladder sooner, lowering the dose).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('120ccf70-623a-56d8-bce9-6f8e78f2a69c', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 31, 31, 'An electron and a positron, both nearly at rest, annihilate. Calculate the total energy released in units of 10⁻¹³ J. Take mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg and c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.64', '10⁻¹³ J', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'E = 2mₑc² = 2 × 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ × (3.00 × 10⁸)² = 1.64 × 10⁻¹³ J. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: two rest masses. C1: E = mc². A1: E = 1.64 × 10⁻¹³ J.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a9ad342a-4751-5f86-8a18-4044935a421c', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 32, 32, 'A PET scan has 300 MBq of tracer in the patient, and 2.0% of the annihilations are recorded as coincidences. How many coincidences are recorded per second?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '6e6', 's⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Rate = 0.020 × 300 × 10⁶ = 6.0 × 10⁶ s⁻¹. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: one annihilation per decay. C1: × 2.0%. A1: rate = 6.0 × 10⁶ s⁻¹.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('c39caa15-9692-5b29-83bc-46cd8dea02fa', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 33, 33, 'How does a PET scanner work out where the tracer is?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Many lines of response cross at the places where annihilations are most frequent; timing places events along each line', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The computer reconstructs the distribution from millions of coincidences. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: lines of response. C1: reconstruction / timing. A1: A (Many lines of response cross at the places where annihilations are most frequent; timing places events along each line).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('5e0278f4-c739-592f-824a-dc085df80dac', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 34, 34, 'Fluorine-18 has a physical half-life of 110 min and is cleared from the body with a biological half-life of 360 min. Calculate the effective half-life, in min, using 1/T(eff) = 1/T(phys) + 1/T(bio).', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '84.26', 'min', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'T = 1 ÷ (1/110 + 1/360) = 84.3 min. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: formula. C1: value. A1: T(eff) = 84.3 min.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('052a8fb8-2bd7-5a20-a365-80276104c9d6', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 35, 35, 'A patient contains 200 MBq of a positron emitter, and every annihilation gives two 0.511 MeV photons. Calculate the total power carried by the photons, in mW. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.0327 mW', 'mW', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'P = 200 × 10⁶ × 1.022 × 10⁶ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 3.270 × 10⁻⁵ W. In mW: 3.270 × 10⁻⁵ × 10³ = 0.0327. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: energy per decay. C1: × activity. A1: P = 0.0327 mW.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('9b3c4636-3290-5c27-9bd7-976ad84f77d5', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 36, 36, 'Why are PET scans often combined with CT scans?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'PET shows where tissue is active and CT shows the anatomy, so together the activity can be located precisely', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Function and structure are overlaid. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: PET functional. C1: CT anatomical. A1: D (PET shows where tissue is active and CT shows the anatomy, so together the activity can be located precisely).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('845a5b65-7b55-5064-84f4-14508780e214', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 37, 37, 'An annihilation occurs 10 cm from the centre, on the line between two opposite detectors. Calculate the difference in arrival times, in ps. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '666.7', 'ps', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Δt = 2 × 0.10 ÷ 3.00 × 10⁸ = 6.667 × 10⁻¹⁰ s. In ps: 6.667 × 10⁻¹⁰ × 10¹² = 667. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: path difference. C1: Δt. A1: Δt = 667 ps.', 3, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg1b32d599-t fg1b32d599-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg1b32d599-t">Off-centre annihilation</title><desc id="fg1b32d599-d">A PET detector ring with an annihilation 10 cm from the centre on the line joining two opposite detectors.</desc><rect x="300" y="163" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="298.1" y="141.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="292.5" y="120.2" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="283.3" y="100.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="270.8" y="82.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="255.3" y="67.2" width="10" heig