stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="175" y="288" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="196.7" y="286.1" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="217.8" y="280.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="237.5" y="271.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="255.3" y="258.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="270.8" y="243.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="283.3" y="225.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="292.5" y="205.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="298.1" y="184.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="180" cy="168" r="60" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="180" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280)">patient</text><line x1="61" y1="168" x2="299" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="205.2" y1="168" x2="68.6" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="63,168 70.3,164.6 70.3,171.4" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="217.2" y1="168" x2="291.4" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="297,168 289.7,171.4 289.7,164.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><circle cx="211.2" cy="168" r="5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="180" cy="168" r="2.4" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><text x="55" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><text x="305" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">B</text><text x="180" y="14" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280)">ring of detectors</text><polygon points="180,194 186.3,191 186.3,197" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="184.9" y1="194" x2="206.3" y2="194" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="211.2,194 204.9,197 204.9,191" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="195.6" y="206" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">10 cm</text></svg>', 'A PET detector ring with an annihilation 10 cm from the centre on the line joining two opposite detectors.'),
('f83dd7ef-2487-52f8-897a-7b72ed6e5c49', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 38, 38, 'How long does it take for the activity of a fluorine-18 dose (half-life 110 min) to fall to 10% of its initial value, in min?', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '365.4', 'min', false, NULL, false, NULL, 't = 110 × ln 10 ÷ ln 2 = 365 min. Mark scheme (4 marks). M1: 0.10 = (½)^(t/t½). C1: take logs. C1: value. A1: t = 365 min.', 4, NULL, NULL),
('b942f87e-16a3-5d37-8732-8c911554186d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 39, 39, 'Why is the fluorine-18 tracer attached to glucose?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Cells that are very active, such as many cancer cells, take up more glucose, so the tracer collects there', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The image shows regions of high metabolism. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: glucose uptake. C1: active tissue highlighted. A1: B (Cells that are very active, such as many cancer cells, take up more glucose, so the tracer collects there).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('baf2ffd7-b536-501e-b6a4-5f623ae894af', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 40, 40, 'A dose of fluorine-18 contains 3.8 × 10¹² nuclei. Taking the mass of one nucleus as 18 u (1 u = 1.66 × 10⁻²⁷ kg), calculate the mass of fluorine-18 in units of 10⁻¹³ kg.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.135', '10⁻¹³ kg', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'm = 3.8 × 10¹² × 18 × 1.66 × 10⁻²⁷ = 1.14 × 10⁻¹³ kg. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: mass of one nucleus. C1: × N. A1: m = 1.14 × 10⁻¹³ kg.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('5b30618f-da9c-5e2e-b452-34e187ea462d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 41, 41, 'Calculate the wavelength of a 0.511 MeV annihilation photon in units of 10⁻¹² m. Take h = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹ and e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.433', '10⁻¹² m', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'λ = hc/E = 6.63 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3.00 × 10⁸ ÷ (0.511 × 10⁶ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹) = 2.43 × 10⁻¹² m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: MeV to J. C1: λ = hc/E. A1: λ = 2.43 × 10⁻¹² m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('f800f28d-8435-5caa-9f8d-a01dadb4ebed', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 42, 42, 'How does the distance a positron travels before annihilating affect a PET image?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'It limits the resolution, because the annihilation is not exactly where the tracer nucleus was', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The positron range blurs the image by about a millimetre. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: positron range. C1: blurring. A1: C (It limits the resolution, because the annihilation is not exactly where the tracer nucleus was).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('a836edf8-a5ab-5fea-a8e8-cee19c8c4e69', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 43, 43, 'A PET coincidence window is 10 ns. How far does light travel in this time? Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '3', 'm', false, NULL, false, NULL, 'd = c × t = 3.00 × 10⁸ × 10 × 10⁻⁹ = 3.0 m. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: d = ct. C1: ns to s. A1: d = 3.0 m.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('404f6196-3aaa-5c6e-8690-cfde25d5d720', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 44, 44, 'Calculate (activity of a fluorine-18 dose 1 hour after injection) ÷ (its activity 2 hours after injection). The half-life is 110 min.', NULL, 2, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.459', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'Ratio = 2^(60 ÷ 110) = 1.46. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: 60 min apart. C1: 2^(t/t½). A1: ratio = 1.46.', 3, NULL, NULL),
('80dff23a-9b82-59b9-a44a-655400ae651d', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 45, 45, 'How are the γ-ray photons detected in a PET scanner?', NULL, 2, 'multiple_choice'::answer_type, 'Scintillator crystals produce flashes of light that photomultipliers turn into electrical pulses', NULL, false, NULL, false, NULL, 'The ring of detectors surrounds the patient. Mark scheme (3 marks). C1: scintillator. C1: photomultiplier. A1: A (Scintillator crystals produce flashes of light that photomultipliers turn into electrical pulses).', 3, NULL, NULL),
('45da8eeb-f237-5f3e-88bc-26e3b2c56fb7', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 46, 46, 'A detector ring has a radius of 0.40 m. An annihilation occurs on the line joining two opposite detectors, and the photon reaching detector A arrives 1.0 ns before the photon reaching B. (a) Calculate the path difference. (b) Calculate the distance of the annihilation from the centre, in cm. (c) State which detector it is nearer. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '15 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) cΔt = 3.00 × 10⁸ × 1.0 × 10⁻⁹ = 0.30 m. (b) d = 0.30 ÷ 2 = 0.15 m, which in cm is 0.15 × 100 = 15. (c) Nearer to A. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: path difference. M1: halve it. C1: value. B1: nearer A. A1: d = 15 cm.', 5, '<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 320" role="img" aria-labelledby="fg0f144758-t fg0f144758-d" style="font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,''Segoe UI'',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:100%;height:auto"><title id="fg0f144758-t">Locating an annihilation</title><desc id="fg0f144758-d">A PET ring of radius 0.40 m. An annihilation on the line between opposite detectors A and B sends photons to both; the photon reaching A arrives 1.0 ns earlier.</desc><rect x="300" y="163" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="298.1" y="141.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="292.5" y="120.2" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="283.3" y="100.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.