yle="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="66.7" y="100.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="57.5" y="120.2" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="51.9" y="141.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="50" y="163" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="51.9" y="184.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="57.5" y="205.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="66.7" y="225.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="79.2" y="243.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="94.7" y="258.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="112.5" y="271.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="132.2" y="280.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="153.3" y="286.1" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="175" y="288" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="196.7" y="286.1" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="217.8" y="280.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="237.5" y="271.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="255.3" y="258.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="270.8" y="243.3" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="283.3" y="225.5" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="292.5" y="205.8" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><rect x="298.1" y="184.7" width="10" height="10" rx="0" style="stroke:currentColor;stroke-width:0.9;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="180" cy="168" r="60" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:4 3"/><text x="180" y="242" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280)">patient</text><line x1="61" y1="168" x2="299" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round;stroke-dasharray:5 4"/><line x1="127.1" y1="168" x2="68.6" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="63,168 70.3,164.6 70.3,171.4" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><line x1="139.1" y1="168" x2="291.4" y2="168" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke-width:2.0;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="297,168 289.7,171.4 289.7,164.6" style="fill:var(--fig-accent-2,#b45309);stroke:none"/><circle cx="133.1" cy="168" r="5" style="stroke:var(--fig-accent,#1d4ed8);stroke-width:2.0;fill:var(--fig-fill,rgba(29,78,216,0.10));stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><circle cx="180" cy="168" r="2.4" style="fill:currentColor;stroke:none"/><text x="55" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">A</text><text x="305" y="146" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor;font-weight:600">B</text><text x="180" y="14" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280)">ring of detectors</text><polygon points="180,194 173.7,197 173.7,191" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><line x1="175.1" y1="194" x2="138" y2="194" style="stroke:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke-width:0.9;fill:none;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round"/><polygon points="133.1,194 139.5,191 139.5,197" style="fill:var(--fig-muted,#6b7280);stroke:none"/><text x="156.6" y="206" font-size="12" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central" style="fill:currentColor">d</text></svg>', 'A PET ring of radius 0.40 m. An annihilation on the line between opposite detectors A and B sends photons to both; the photon reaching A arrives 1.0 ns earlier.'),
('f27b6a28-83c8-588f-8141-cba778f5e710', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 47, 47, 'Fluorine-18 (half-life 110 min) is made in a cyclotron 1.5 hours'' drive from the hospital. A patient needs 400 MBq at injection, 30 min after the tracer arrives. (a) Calculate the total time from production to injection. (b) Calculate the activity that must leave the cyclotron, in MBq.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '852', 'MBq', false, NULL, false, ARRAY['8.52e8']::text[], '(a) 90 + 30 = 120 min. (b) A₀ = 400 × 2^(120 ÷ 110) = 852 MBq. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: total time. M1: A₀ = A × 2^(t/t½). C1: exponent. C1: value. B1: decay during transport and waiting. A1: A₀ = 852 MBq.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('97a1e4b2-de8d-55a1-a0c2-25b7c045edde', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 48, 48, 'A positron and an electron, both at rest, annihilate. (a) Calculate the energy of each photon in J. (b) Calculate the momentum of each photon. (c) Show that the total momentum is zero. Give only the answer to (b), in units of 10⁻²² kg m s⁻¹. Take mₑ = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ kg and c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '2.733', '10⁻²² kg m s⁻¹', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) E = mₑc² = 9.11 × 10⁻³¹ × (3.00 × 10⁸)² = 8.199 × 10⁻¹⁴ J. (b) p = E/c = 8.199 × 10⁻¹⁴ ÷ 3.00 × 10⁸ = 2.73 × 10⁻²² kg m s⁻¹. (c) The photons travel in opposite directions with equal momenta. Mark scheme (5 marks). C1: photon energy. M1: p = E/c. C1: value. B1: opposite directions. A1: p = 2.73 × 10⁻²² kg m s⁻¹.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('84aecdb2-bcf3-5b32-94a5-9586af26ee32', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 49, 49, 'A patient receives 370 MBq of fluorine-18 (λ = 1.05 × 10⁻⁴ s⁻¹). Each decay deposits, on average, 0.25 MeV from the positron in the body. (a) Calculate the total number of decays. (b) Calculate the total energy deposited by the positrons, in J. Take e = 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ C.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '0.141', 'J', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) N₀ = A₀/λ = 370 × 10⁶ ÷ 1.05 × 10⁻⁴ = 3.524 × 10¹². (b) E = 3.524 × 10¹² × 0.25 × 10⁶ × 1.60 × 10⁻¹⁹ = 0.141 J. Mark scheme (6 marks). M1: all nuclei eventually decay. C1: N₀ = A₀/λ. C1: energy per decay in J. M1: multiply. C1: value. A1: E = 0.141 J.', 6, NULL, NULL),
('1aebba15-24eb-5f00-a552-880310d2b5ed', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 50, 50, 'A PET scanner can measure arrival-time differences to within 300 ps. (a) Calculate the corresponding uncertainty in position along the line of response. (b) Comment on whether timing alone can give a sharp image. Give only the answer to (a), in cm. Take c = 3.00 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '4.5 cm', 'cm', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) Δx = cΔt/2 = 3.00 × 10⁸ × 300 × 10⁻¹² ÷ 2 = 0.045 m, which in cm is 0.045 × 100 = 4.5. (b) No: 4.5 cm is coarse, so many crossing lines of response are still needed. Mark scheme (5 marks). M1: Δx = cΔt/2. C1: substitution. C1: value. B1: comment. A1: Δx = 4.5 cm.', 5, NULL, NULL),
('fe08a837-b06f-54cc-9ab1-c448f950489a', '1fd2e146-9233-4bc7-8fd2-b600f61a7d73', '36e936df-9896-57b6-a5e3-651ca3d785ed', 'a-level', '30.8', '9702 coursebook 30.8 · PET scanning', 51, 51, 'Fluorine-18 decays by β⁺ emission to oxygen-18. (a) State the proton number of oxygen if fluorine has 9. (b) The decay releases 0.63 MeV, and the positron then annihilates (photons 0.511 MeV each). Calculate the total energy released per decay, in MeV. (c) Explain why the annihilation photons, not the positrons, are detected.', NULL, 3, 'numeric'::answer_type, '1.652', 'MeV', false, NULL, false, NULL, '(a) 9 − 1 = 8. (b) E = 0.63 + 2 × 0.511 = 1.652 MeV. (c) Positrons travel only about 1 mm in tissue; γ-photons escape the body. Mark scheme (6 marks). C1: Z = 8. C1: annihilation energy. M1: add decay energy. C1: value. B1: photons escape, positrons do not. A1: E = 1.652 MeV.', 6, NULL, NULL)
